snippet.textDisplay:
@wreynolds1995 That’s a stupid comparison. The robot isn’t programmed to “get objects from container A to container B by any means necessary”

It’s programmed to remove objects in handfuls from container A and place them in container B. The task isn’t given to the robot as a puzzle to solve, it’s given to the robot to test its spatial awareness, object manipulation and hand coordination.

It could be programmed to lift and dump the box, too. It’s just doing what it’s told within the parameters laid out for it in its programming.

