@Merc30043 AI is definitely a good thing that comes with some dangers. Every good technology faces enormous backlash from luddites. I can't think of any tech ever that didn't go through a phase of hatred from self-aggrandized "wise" people. Gasoline was considered useless. Phones were considered an unprofitable venture. Windows/Mac was refused by nearly every major tech company. I couldn't possibly know, but I'd take an educated guess that the first person to purposely light a fire was probably not well appreciated.

It's only a matter of time that my argument stands for itself - in fact I think that time has already come but some people are not aware enough of the technology and its capabilities to pass any form of credible judgement.

You can argue in your infinite wisdom that AI is not great, but let's see what happens when you don't have a job because someone embracing AI does your job 1000x over. 🤷‍♂We'll move on without you, just like we always do.

