@bensalvador113 Just really flawed logic in general. You judge a technology in its infancy, then re-judge whenever it gets an upgrade. VR sucked when it was first made. And it sucked for the next 5-6 attempts at VR for the next 40 years afterward. And people were right to say it sucked. And it's STILL in a barely usable state with lots of inherent flaws that need to be worked out.

Current AI art/animation is in that first release phase. And it sucks. And I will judge it as it is currently. If it's better later, I may reappraise. but right now it sucks, and no amount of deluding yourself into thinking it doesn't, or coping that it will be better later, so you have to be an early adopter will change that.

Basically, early adoption is for suckers and grifters. If you aren't making a quick buck off a new technology you need to really do a deep think on what it actually does for you before you invest in it.

