snippet.textDisplay:
@TumpalManurung A good enough AI could verify all the conclusions in research papers and also verify if the used methods are good for the declared results.

Basically do the same thing as peer review should have done. Plus re-calculate all results because in most cases human implemented peer review bindly assumes that calculations have been executed correctly. This is because peer review is already a pretty slow process and the more complete verification you do, the slower it would get.

AGI level AI can do all that and it should be cheaper to use than humans so you can afford to re-calculate everything.

