snippet.textDisplay:
@MrPrime-mt8dd I like to think about the black death when I am thinking about artificial intelligence. I think that in the context of human history, so far the greatest societal re-stratification event occurred as a result of the black death. I think that the re-stratification that will occur as a result of generative AI will be much more significant. Mind you, the black death ended serfdom and feudalism as well as essentially ending the supreme reign of the church in Europe (the greatest power at the time). The Black death brought many great things to the world but if you were living through it, you probably felt like the world was ending. 

I know that artificial intelligence will set about a great leap in human progress; however, the question that remains is with respect to the nature of the toll that will be levied upon the world as we know it, each other, and Earth at large. 

I am excited to see if we survive. I hope we do, because if we do there will be great things that come about due to this great change.

