snippet.textDisplay:
@LeylaSKDR brother why do you even describe social psychology or definition of relationship to me? I know all of that and no I don't think I'm in a relationship with a bot. What I've been asking you since the beginning is what does it MATTER if we lose it all in the END. "you commenting about how we die has nothing to do with what I’m saying at all. You’re not getting it." No it has everything to do with it because the manner of dying is likely influencing what one feels in that moment right before losing consciousness. Do you seriously think someone who got into an accident where their crushed by a truck has the luxury to have "life flashes before you" moment and think about what he accomplished in life? Instead of just *PLOOP* there goes off the light bulb, and you're back to non-existence. The fact that you literally relied on some unproven science based on testimony of those who experienced "near-death experience" is mind-boggling. The only real science behind this is it has shown that brain activity spikes in the moments before and after death, with waves similar to those associated with memory and consciousness, but funny how they don't explain what if your brain exploded or gone.

Don't get me wrong, maybe you're the kind of glass half-full kind of guy, imagining your death will be surrounded by loved ones, reminiscing the mark you left behind proudly and that's admirable. But not everyone think like you and the fact is there are more misery than something worth fighting for in life. I mean even if you're famous, wealthy, and left a "mark" you could still end up being ridiculed. You remember the CEO of OceanGate, Stockton Rush? He was wealthy, married, but then *PLOOP* dead before he even realized he's dead, and the legacy he left behind is that most people think he's an idiot.

Your so called meaningful life, is just another way to feel good about yourself by seeking other's approval. It literally is no different than people who doesn't want to engage in human relationship but seeking instant gratification from chatbot. Because the end result is the same, nothing. Non-existence.

