snippet.textDisplay:
@chasing.thund3r You have no idea how AI works or you're just AI bro.  First off, this AI is an LLM, not AGI, which has been admitted by some known figures in AI industry. 

Second, AI is an imitation of a small portion of human brain, not entire brain. Nobody has ever accomplished to build entire human brain from scratch, or a machine that has ALL functions as human brain has. That's a known fact. You can simply learn about parietal, temporal, frontal, and occipital lobes of human brain, and compare all of them to AI. You'll realize how different humans are from AI.

AGI might resemble more to human brains (even that would be vastly different from human brains) while this AI is far from how human think, react, and decide.

